      ":question/problem": "Find the antiderivative of\n$-3x^{3}-\\frac{4}{x^{6}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[5]{x^{6}}}.$ For real $x\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int\\left(-3x^{3}-\\frac{4}{x^{6}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[5]{x^{6}}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int\\left(-3x^{3}-4x^{-6}+x^{\\frac{-6}{5}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= -3\\int x^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x-4\\int x^{-6}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\int x^{\\frac{-6}{5}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= -3\\left(\\frac{x^{3+1}}{(3+1)}\\right)-4\\left(\\frac{x^{-6+1}}{(-6+1)}\\right)\\\\ &\\quad +\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{-6}{5}+1}}{(\\frac{-6}{5}+1)}\\right)+C\\\\ &= -\\frac{3x^{4}}{4}+\\frac{4}{5x^{5}}-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt[5]{x}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
