      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int\\left(\\frac{5}{\\sqrt[7]{x^{8}}}-\\frac{4}{x^{2}}+4x^{4}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int\\left(5x^{\\frac{-8}{7}}-4x^{-2}+4x^{4}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= 5\\int x^{\\frac{-8}{7}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x-4\\int x^{-2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+4\\int x^{4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= 5\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{-8}{7}+1}}{(\\frac{-8}{7}+1)}\\right)-4\\left(\\frac{x^{-2+1}}{(-2+1)}\\right)\\\\ &\\quad +4\\left(\\frac{x^{4+1}}{(4+1)}\\right)+C\\\\ &= -\\frac{35}{\\sqrt[7]{x}}+\\frac{4}{x}+\\frac{4x^{5}}{5}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
